event: response.output_text.done
data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_0a6f517af0616dc3016ac2717f8ab881908c5648fe66a4975f","logprobs":[],"output_index":3,"sequence_number":286,"text":"Since \\(p>1000\\) is an odd prime, and \\(p+2\\) cannot be divisible by 3, \\(p\\equiv5\\pmod 6\\). The candidates therefore go \\(1001,1007,\\ldots\\), in steps of 6.\n\nBefore 1091, each candidate fails: \\(1001=7\\cdot143\\), \\(1007=19\\cdot53\\); for 1013, 1019, 1043, 1049, and 1079, respectively, \\(p+2\\) or \\(p+6\\) is divisible by 5; \\(1025\\) and \\(1055\\) are divisible by 5; \\(1031+6=1037=17\\cdot61\\); \\(1061+6=1067=11\\cdot97\\); and \\(1073=29\\cdot37\\).\n\nFor \\(p=1091\\), all three numbers \\(1091,1093,1097\\) have no prime divisor at most 33 (their square roots are below 34), so all are prime. Thus the smallest such prime is **1091**.\n\nIts last digit is 1, so I checked weather for **Y, France**, a one-letter commune: **14°C, rain**."}

